    "9c39068141798683788e80d6a0cecb": {
      "source_id": "US-HI:service:70db2b1f2445",
      "authority_type": "court_rule",
      "citation": "Haw. R. Civ. P. 4(c)",
      "text": "(c) Same: By whom served. Service of al l process shall be made: (1) anywhere in the State by the sheriff or the sheriff's deputy, by some other person specially appointed by the court for that purpose, or by any person who is not a party and is not less than 18 years of age; or (2) in any county by the chief of police or the chief's duly authorized subordinate. A subpoena, however, may be served as provided in Rule 45.",
